WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.140
If your heart swelled three sizes watching
The Grinch, you'll want to make sure you caught

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.819
all the amazing hidden details.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:11.700
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today, I'm going to reveal 17 cool easter

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.509
eggs and references you might have missed
in Illumination's new animated movie!

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:19.960
Keep watching to the end to find out The Grinch's
secret connection to Gru from the Despicable

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.160
Me movies!

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.109
And subscribe and leave a comment about the
film for a chance to win some awesome Grinch

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:26.460
merchandise.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.779
The Grinch has a ton of fabulous gadgets and
inventions he puts to use in his mission to

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:32.540
steal Christmas from Whoville.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.550
In one particular tribute to the animated
TV special, we see the Grinch employ some

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.530
springy type of stilts which enable him to
jump with ease from one rooftop to another

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.260
as he gathers up the Whos' presents.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.680
The new Grinch movie tips its hat to Dr Seuss,
the author of the original book, in the scene

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.309
where the Grinch starts making his Santa Claus
disguise.

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:55.930
Look carefully at the model of the sewing
machine which is "Theodor", a shout-out to

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.309
Dr. Seuss's real name Theodor Geisel.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:03.340
A funny little detail you might have missed
is the title of the book that the Grinch tosses

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:07.120
at the alarm clock when it wakes him up playing
cheery Christmas songs.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.640
The book is called "Spelunking For Beginners"
which is very appropriate for the Grinch as

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.950
"spelunking" refers to the activity or hobby
of exploring caves, and the Grinch, of course,

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.500
lives in a cave on Mount Crumpit.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.040
One of the roles that Benedict Cumberbatch,
who voices the Grinch, is best known for is

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.229
Marvel's Doctor Strange.

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:29.050
And there's a very cool visual nod to Cumberbatch's
Sorcerer Supreme in an atmospheric scene in

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:30.390
the new Grinch movie.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:34.759
After the holiday-hating character comes up
with his "wonderful, awful idea" to steal

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:39.689
Christmas, we see him walk up the stairs of
his cave-home and stand in front of a circular

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:40.689
window.

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:44.920
It's not exactly the same, but the lines across
the round window and the circular centre do

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.820
bring to mind the Window of the Worlds in
Dr Strange's Sanctum Santorum.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:54.130
In the original book and animated TV special,
as well as stealing all the Whos' presents,

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.530
the Grinch also takes all their food, "even
the last can of Who hash!"

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:03.010
And there's a little call-back to that in
Illumination's new movie when the Grinch realises

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:08.009
he's eaten all the groceries he bought to
last him through to January, even his "emergency

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:09.610
stash of Who hash".

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:13.910
And when he goes into Whoville to restock,
he sweeps a whole load of Who-hash cans off

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.580
the shelf and into his basket.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:21.280
When Cindy-Lou first bumps into the Grinch,
she's on her way to post a letter to Santa.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.480
Which is a nice hat-tip to how in the live-action
movie, Cindy-Lou's father was a postmaster

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.650
and she happened to meet the Grinch for the
first time at the town's post office.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:34.310
In the new Grinch movie, Cindy-Lou's hairstyle
with its two braids sticking up with pink

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:39.290
bows is a lovely reference to the original
book, where Cindy-Lou had two wiry strands

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:44.550
of hair sticking up on her head, and it's
also a cool shout-out to the 1960s TV special,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.480
where she wore two pink bows in her hair.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.201
Something that infuriates the Grinch even
more than usual is when he discovers from

00:02:51.201 --> 00:02:55.070
his nearest neighbour Mr Bricklebaum that
the mayor of Whoville wants Christmas to be

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.060
three times bigger this year.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.959
And this is a subtle little nod to how the
Grinch's heart will eventually grow three

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:03.640
sizes by the end of the story.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:08.300
When the Grinch wants to learn all about how
to become like Santa for his dastardly plan,

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:12.140
he starts flipping through a book called "Cringle's
Christmas Almanac".

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.110
The name Kris Kringle, when spelled with a
'K', is an alternate name for Santa Claus,

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:19.940
and you may well have heard that name before
if you've ever watched the classic Christmas

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.150
movie Miracle on 34th Street.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:27.100
When Fred the reindeer, who was originally
going to pull the Grinch's sleigh, ends up

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:31.069
leaving, the Grinch references the classic
song "Rudolph, the Red-Nosed Reindeer".

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:35.049
Riffing on a line from that famous Christmas
tune, the Grinch promotes Max to reindeer

00:03:35.049 --> 00:03:38.580
duty, saying "you will guide my sleight tonight".

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.720
The single antler that the Grinch places on
Max's head is also a little throwback to the

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.580
same thing that happened in the book, the
animated TV special, and the live-action film.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:52.319
This time, Max's antler has been enhanced
with an extendable arm to grab the swag that

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:56.390
the Grinch tosses down to him during the great
Christmas heist.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:00.629
And as the Grinch orders Max to get to work,
there's a funny moment as the little dog pulls

00:04:00.629 --> 00:04:05.020
at the enormous sleigh and, instead of moving
it forward, he just ends up burrowing down

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:10.209
into the snow, before he finally summons enough
strength to pull himself up and set off.

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:14.099
It's an amusing moment which echoes a similar
scene in the TV special where the Grinch's

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:18.870
sleigh was so laden with everything he'd stolen
from Whoville, that Max just couldn't get

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:23.130
himself up out of the snow and stayed like
that pretty much all the way back to Mount

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.380
Crumpit!

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:28.270
A little difference in the new Grinch movie
is that in this version the Grinch steals

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:32.840
Christmas from Cindy-Lou's house last of all,
whereas in all the other versions, her home

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.560
is the first stop on his yuletide raid.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:40.030
The new film does, however, acknowledge the
original order as the metre on the Grinch's

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.020
sleigh counts down the number of houses he's
robbed and when he gets to Cindy-Lou's home,

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:46.550
the metre reads "number 1".

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.280
The new movie also has a couple of easter
eggs to another of Dr Seuss's most famous

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.110
books, The Cat in the Hat.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:56.620
In The Grinch, the green grump wears a red
and white-striped scarf when he goes food-shopping

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:01.590
in Whoville and he also dons a red and white
stripy tie when he visits Cindy-Lou's house

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:06.030
and both of these echo the Cat in the Hat's
iconic stripy red and white hat.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.840
As an Illumination film, The Grinch also has
a number of hat-tips to previous movies by

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:12.080
the animation studio.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:17.111
In Despicable Me 3, we already saw Margot
wearing a Grinch on one of her shirts and

00:05:17.111 --> 00:05:20.930
the clothing-related connections between the
movies continue in this latest film.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:26.220
First up is the stripy dark-coloured scarf
that the Grinch wears during his raid on Mr

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.220
Bricklebaum's house.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:31.260
The Grinch's muffler looks an awful lot like
Gru's signature scarf from the Despicable

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.260
Me movies.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:36.370
There's also a nod to Agnes's fluffy unicorn
obsession in The Grinch.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:40.490
As the Whos get their Christmas photos taken,
you can see that Groopert's family are also

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:45.900
fans of fluffy unicorns, though their one
has blue rather than pink hair like Agnes's.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.570
And Cindy-Lou's friend Izzy also has a similar
toy unicorn by her bed.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:55.199
If you were wondering who narrated the new
Grinch movie, well it's none other than singer-songwriter

00:05:55.199 --> 00:05:56.199
Pharrell Williams.

00:05:56.199 --> 00:06:00.900
He's a regular contributor to Illumination's
movies and composed numerous themes and songs,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:04.280
including the Oscar-nominated Happy, for the
Despicable Me movies.

